# Every text file is stored as LF in the repository AND checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# `eol=lf` is the part that matters on Windows: without it, a contributor with git's
# core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF working tree on checkout, and the next editor save pushes
# CRLF back through — producing commits whose entire content is a line-ending flip. This
# repo has had one of those, a commit whose message described source changes but whose only
# actual content was docs/index.html re-saved with different endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files git must never line-ending-convert or try to diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
